). The ṛṣi (the sage to whom it is revealed) is अगस्त्य. The devatā (deity to which it is addressed) is Annastuti. The छन्दस् or meter is mostly Anuṣṭubh.
According to the sage शौनक (vide Ṛgvidhāna 1-27) this सूक्त must be chanted daily at the time of ड़ोओद्. Such chanting purifies the ड़ोओद्, destroying whatever impurities may be there, and ensures health and energy.
The first verse is introductory. The second verse supplicates ड़ोओद् for protection. The third requests ड़ोओद् to be palatable. The next three are verses of praise. The seventh verse requests ड़ोओद् to be available in plenty when it rains. The next three verses urge the body to grow strong as a result of consuming ड़ोओद्. The last verse is a praise to ड़ोओद् in the form of सोम.
